ue" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fbd9682298969335dcbc8e0642bf48e91a65c8ef4512ffd363f581f65504528" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2n\\pi )=1}$\n- $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2q\\pi )=1}$\n- $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x\\pi )=1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fbd9682298969335dcbc8e0642bf48e91a65c8ef4512ffd363f581f65504528" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements. \n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x\\pi )=1$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2m\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}+m,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is finite. There are no values of $m\\in Z$ such that $\\frac{1}{4}+m\\in Z.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nA={}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|A|=0,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nB={…,-\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{5}{4},\\frac{9}{4},…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ and $C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fbd9682298969335dcbc8e0642bf48e91a65c8ef4512ffd363f581f65504528" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e146cf3342d1a448b3bcc321380e2d6f73a85d06a1d9ec18bdd36ec307186b3d" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fbd9682298969335dcbc8e0642bf48e91a65c8ef4512ffd363f581f65504528" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fbd9682298969335dcbc8e0642bf48e91a65c8ef4512ffd363f581f65504528" "basis" 1424 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040284/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "